# Host storage locations. These must be absolute paths — stay-go renders this
# project into a private cache dir before each run, so the upstream "./volume"
# style relative mount would land in the cache and be lost on the next apply.

# Scrypted database, plugin installs, settings. Small but must persist — losing
# it means reconfiguring every camera and plugin from scratch.
SCRYPTED_VOLUME=/storage/apps/scrypted/volume

# Video recordings (Scrypted NVR). Kept on the pool alongside frigate's, under
# the security tree so both NVRs' footage lives in one place.
SCRYPTED_NVR=/storage/security/scrypted

TZ=America/Phoenix

# Host GIDs for the GPU device nodes, resolved on the target host at config load
# time. These are passed to group_add as NUMBERS: docker resolves group_add
# names against the container's /etc/group, and the Scrypted image has no
# "render" group, so the name form fails the container create with
#   Error response from daemon: Unable to find group render
#
# The `|| echo 0` fallback matters — without it a missing group would render an
# empty string and produce an invalid `group_add: [""]`, which fails the same
# way but with a much less obvious message. GID 0 (root) is a safe no-op here
# because the Scrypted container already runs as root.
RENDER_GID=$(getent group render | cut -d: -f3 || echo 0)
VIDEO_GID=$(getent group video | cut -d: -f3 || echo 0)
